          "text": "\n\nPerfect! All tests pass successfully. Let me provide a final summary:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the required changes to fix the bpfman RPC server startup issues:\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n1. **Socket Directory Creation** (`bpfman-api/src/bin/rpc/serve.rs`):\n   - Automatically creates the socket directory before attempting to bind the socket\n   - Extracts the parent directory from the socket path and creates it using `create_dir_all()`\n   - Creates the CSI socket sub-directory when `--csi-support` flag is enabled\n   - Provides clear error messages with context if directory creation fails\n\n2. **Logging Initialization** (both `bpfman-api/src/bin/rpc/main.rs` and `bpfman/src/bin/cli/main.rs`):\n   - Added `init_logging()` function that initializes logging at startup\n   - Detects if running under systemd using `connected_to_journal()`\n   - Uses `JournalLog` for systemd journal integration when available\n   - Falls back to `env_logger` for standard output logging otherwise\n   - Added `manage_journal_log_level()` function to parse `RUST_LOG` environment variable\n   - Reports invalid `RUST_LOG` values to stderr without panicking\n   - Adds binary-specific metadata to journal logs (\"bpfman-rpc\" or \"bpfman\")\n\n### Test Results:\n\n✅ Socket directory `/run/bpfman-sock/` is created automatically  \n✅ Socket file `bpfman.sock` is created successfully  \n✅ Custom socket paths work correctly  \n✅ CSI socket directory `/run/bpfman/csi/` is created when `--csi-support` is enabled  \n✅ Logging works with `RUST_LOG` environment variable  \n✅ Both RPC and CLI binaries initialize logging properly  \n✅ Invalid log levels are reported without causing panics  \n\nThe implementation follows the existing codebase patterns and uses the already-available dependencies (`systemd-journal-logger`, `env_logger`, `log`).",
